This was the moment where I realised I couldn’t go ahead with the process I’d planned. I couldn’t rely on these printers to print good books. All that work to get the book magically connected to the book distribution industry had been wasted time. It was time to think of a new plan."]},{"segments":["The first print run sold out in less than 2 days. I phoned Rik and ordered some more. They lasted to the end of the week.

